  "text": "Two billionaire friends that were airline company rivals agreed to a crazy bet. Not only did they both own competing airline companies, but they were also owners of Formula One teams that would compete in an upcoming race. They weren't your typical billionaires. These two wanted to put their egos on the line, so they arranged the bet. Whoever's team finishes last would have to dress as a female flight attendant and serve passengers on a real flight, on the winner's airline. So when Richard Branson's team came last, He kept his word, he shaved his legs, but not his beard, put on lipstick, heels, and the full Air Asia uniform that boarded the flight. He did the whole safety demo, and even served drinks. But when he was giving juice to one passenger, he realized that it wasn't just any passenger, it was Tony Fernandez, the man he had lost the bet to. So naturally, he accidentally spilled an entire tray of orange juice on him. Tony ended up spending the rest of the flight in his underwear. On his own airplane. Man, if I'm ever rich, I want to be like these."
